# Who must review what (FR-PROJ-01). Replace the two teams with yours.
#
# Review routing is the control that keeps a model change and a production
# change apart, so it has to cover everything that decides what runs in CI and
# what ships, not just the specs: a pull request that touches only a workflow,
# `profiles.yml` or `scoring/` would otherwise need no team's approval at all.
# When you add a top-level file or directory, add a line for it here.
#
# The DS team owns what a model is made of.
/models/           @your-org/ds-team
/datasets/         @your-org/ds-team
/sources.yml       @your-org/ds-team
/macros/           @your-org/ds-team
/tests/            @your-org/ds-team

# MLOps owns where and how it runs, and what reaches production.
/promotions.yml    @your-org/mlops-team
/scoring/          @your-org/mlops-team
/profiles.yml      @your-org/mlops-team
/mbt_project.yml   @your-org/mlops-team
/packages.yml      @your-org/mlops-team
/requirements.in   @your-org/mlops-team
/requirements.txt  @your-org/mlops-team
/scripts/          @your-org/mlops-team
/.github/          @your-org/mlops-team
/.woodpecker/      @your-org/mlops-team
/renovate.json     @your-org/mlops-team
/.pre-commit-config.yaml @your-org/mlops-team
/CODEOWNERS        @your-org/mlops-team

# Deliberately unowned: README.md and .gitignore.
